Rules:
  [R1] Use Next.js for SSR/SSG and routing.
  [R2] Use Module Federation for micro-frontend architecture.
  [R3] Use monorepo (Turborepo/Nx) for shared packages.
  [R4] Implement feature-based folder structure.
  [R5] Use Atomic Design for component hierarchy.
  [R6] Implement error boundaries for error handling.
  [R7] Use Suspense for async data loading.
  [R8] Implement proper SEO with metadata API.

Pros:
  - Scalable architecture
  - Team independence
  - Better performance

Cons:
  - Complexity
  - Build configuration
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Vue
  - Angular
  - SvelteKit

State: +

